    "q-3800": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3800",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the solutions of $-2{d}^{2}-32=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{d}^{2}-32 & =0 \\\\ -2{d}^{2} & =32 \\\\ {d}^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nd=\\pm \\sqrt{-16}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $d$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\pm \\sqrt{-16} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
