    "q-112392": {
      "dom_id": "step-q112392",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Solve the equation $64{x}^{2}+25=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ 64{x}^{2} & =-25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{25}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
