    "q-66254": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66254",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the solutions of the equation $25{z}^{2}+36=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{z}^{2}+36 & =0 \\\\ 25{z}^{2} & =-36 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =-\\frac{36}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nz=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{36}{25}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{36}{25}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{36}{25}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{36}{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{36}}{\\sqrt{25}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{6}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
