    "q-54630": {
      "dom_id": "step-q54630",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "What are the solutions of the equation $8{y}^{2}+12=0?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{y}^{2}+12 & =0 \\\\ 8{y}^{2} & =-12 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{12}{8} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{3}{2}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-54630-a",
